From 12cdd8b9c54f72f4a286d8cf5620a094b1e09384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Gathondu <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:17:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-rounds): keep the decision at each fork with a week
 sent (RR29)

paulgsc/some-ui#3257 (RR29), with the phone's send in some-ui's RR25 D2:
a week sent may carry `verdicts`, the owner's decision at each fork of a
/2 week, each named `<week>:<ticket>:<n>:verdict` beside the fork's take,
`<week>:<ticket>:<n>`: a listed option by id, their own (which the fork's
take says), or, for a fork left alone, the recommended by default (C693).
Its shape is the essay's DecisionSchema, less an own option's words.

- read_sent refuses a ref that names no fork of the week's tickets (fork
  from 1, up to the ticket's points), one an earlier decision names, an
  option id that isn't a capital A to F, and a decision of any other kind
  or with keys it doesn't take. Home doesn't hold a fork's options: the
  phone picks only among them.
- The week's record (GET /rust-weeks/:id/record, and the mailbox's rust
  index) gives each ticket's `decisions`, by fork; empty for a /1 week.
- No table changes: the decisions are part of the send's body, stored as
  the draft and the final already are. A phone from before sends none.
- CONTRACT_EPOCH 23 -> 24, a payload change a client needs (23 is RR23's
  diagnostics); the image's provides label follows.

